// One-off: records GDD v0.41 (general perks back on the weapon hub, balance of the per-gun perks).
const fs = require('fs');
const f = process.argv[2];
let t = fs.readFileSync(f, 'utf8');
const r = (a, b) => { const n = t.split(a).length - 1; if (n !== 1) throw new Error(n + ' x ' + a.slice(0, 60)); t = t.split(a).join(b); };
r('Status: **v0.40, 2026-11-13**', 'Status: **v0.41, 2026-11-13**');
r('- v0.40 (2026-11-13): owner chose **perks per gun**',
	'- v0.41 (2026-11-13): owner: **Marksman, Precision Recovery and Arcane Conduit are general again, as at first** (they work on every gun, Marksman also on the staff and the sword) and sit on the weapon hub with Heavy Rounds; Deadeye stays next to Marksman (they stack, as before); Tight Choke stays. The architect measured every weapon perk with the balance tool (new table "what one point buys") and tuned the new per-gun perks to the existing ones: **Rapid Reload -15% per rank** on each gun (was -10% on all guns at once), **Tight Choke -15%** per rank. Arcane Conduit needs only Heavy Rounds now. Details in §18 "Weapon tree".\n- v0.40 (2026-11-13): owner chose **perks per gun**');
r('- **Weapon tree, v0.40 (owner: "perks per gun"):**',
	'- **Weapon tree, v0.41 (owner: the three general perks stay general):** **Hub page:** Heavy Rounds (+10% gun damage, all guns) in the middle; Marksman (+0.25x head / weak point damage with every weapon, staff and sword included, 2 points per rank) -> Precision Recovery (2 points per rank) on the left; Arcane Conduit (+10% elemental build-up from enchanted weapons per rank, needs Heavy Rounds) on the right; the three gun emblems hang from Heavy Rounds. **Every gun page:** its own Quick Trigger (-8% time between shots of that gun per rank) -> Rapid Reload (**-15%** reload time per rank, -45% at 3) and Steady Grip (-20% recoil). **Pistol:** Deadeye (+0.25x pistol head damage; it stacks with Marksman as it always did). **Rifle:** Long Shot. **Shotgun:** Point Blank -> Tight Choke (**-15%** pellet spread, hip and aimed, per rank). All 3 ranks, 1 point per rank unless said.\n'
	+ '  - **Balance (architect, `Tools/Balance/balance_model.js`, table "what one point buys"):** each perk alone at full rank on top of Heavy Rounds 3, as expected damage per second of its gun. The unconditional one-gun perks the owner already had buy +5% (Deadeye) to +7% (Quick Trigger) per point; Heavy Rounds +11% per point on all three guns at once; the range perks +17% (Long Shot) and +20% (Point Blank), but only at their best range. The new per-gun Rapid Reload at -10% bought only +2.6% to +4.2%, so it goes to -15% (+4.1% pistol, +6.8% rifle, +5.1% shotgun). The model now also counts accuracy: a provisional share of each gun\'s misses comes from recoil (pistol 30%, rifle 50%, shotgun 15%) and from spread (15%, 20%, 50%). With it, Steady Grip buys +6.7% on the rifle but only +2% on the pistol and +1% on the shotgun, and Tight Choke at -15% buys +2.5%. Those are the weak spots; replacing them is the owner\'s call.\n'
	+ '- **Weapon tree, v0.40 (superseded by v0.41 above; owner: "perks per gun"):**');
fs.writeFileSync(f, t);
console.log('ok');

