	'- v0.42 (2026-11-13): owner chose three perk changes the architect proposed from the balance table: the pistol\'s Steady Grip becomes **Quick Draw** (aim 20% faster and move 10% faster while aiming, per rank), the shotgun\'s Steady Grip becomes **Extended Tube** (more shells), and the rifle gets **Extended Mag** (+5 rounds per magazine per rank). Measuring them showed that a bigger magazine also carries more ammo (spare magazines hold the bigger magazine; the shotgun\'s reserve is magazines x tube size), so the architect set Extended Tube to **+1 shell per rank** instead of the +2 shown to the owner: +2 doubled the shells carried, twice any other perk. Details in §18 "Weapon tree".\n- v0.41 (2026-11-13): owner: **Marksman');
r('- **Weapon tree, v0.41 (owner: the three general perks stay general):**',
	'- **Weapon tree, v0.42 (owner\'s perk choices):** as v0.41 below, with three changes. **Pistol:** Steady Grip is replaced by **Quick Draw** (aim time x0.8 and +0.1 move speed while aiming, per rank: aiming takes 60% less time and no longer slows the player at rank 3). **Rifle:** new **Extended Mag** under Long Shot (+5 rounds per magazine per rank, 30 -> 45; spare magazines are the bigger size too): +4.8% damage per second per point and +50% damage of the full load at rank 3, the same per point as Long Shot\'s load gain. **Shotgun:** Steady Grip is replaced by **Extended Tube** (+1 shell per rank, 6 -> 9; the reserve grows with it): +3.6% per point and +50% load, like Extended Mag. Provisional: +2 shells per rank (the number the owner saw when choosing) gave +100% load, double any other perk, so it is +1 until the owner says otherwise. All 1 point per rank, 3 ranks.\n- **Weapon tree, v0.41 (owner: the three general perks stay general; partly superseded by v0.42 above):**');
fs.writeFileSync(f, t);
console.log('ok');

